1	//! A journal of foreground work and the semantic boundaries between activity intervals.
2	//!
3	//! The foreground thread records task polls, action handlers, input dispatches,
4	//! draws, and presentations as [`ForegroundEvent`]s in a bounded journal ring.
5	//! Task polls shorter than [`TASK_POLL_FLOOR`] are folded into summaries, which
6	//! bound the stream by the number of slow polls while preserving their exact
7	//! count and total duration.
8	//!
9	//! Presentation and the foreground going idle are explicit [`IntervalBoundary`]
10	//! entries in the same stream. Independent [`ForegroundJournalCollector`]s
11	//! feed entries to [`IntervalSealer`], a pure state machine that groups all work
12	//! preceding each boundary into a [`FrameSnapshot`]. The sealer does not infer
13	//! boundaries from elapsed time or from incidental event kinds such as draws.
14	
15	use std::cell::{RefCell, UnsafeCell};
16	use std::collections::{HashMap, VecDeque};
17	use std::mem::MaybeUninit;
18	use std::sync::{
19	    Arc,
20	    atomic::{AtomicU64, AtomicUsize, Ordering},
21	};
22	use std::time::Duration;
23	
24	use scheduler::Instant;
25	
26	use super::{ActionTiming, FrameTiming, PresentTiming, TaskTiming};
27	use crate::WindowId;
